{"step_index":120,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T07:07:13Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# UMGN - Production & Cloud Deployment Guide\n\nUMGN is a production-ready, highly secure personal AI chatbot application. This guide explains how to run UMGN locally, configure external AI providers, enforce HTTPS with Caddy, and scale from a personal/small-team deployment (10 users) to enterprise cloud scale (10,000+ users).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Quick Start (Local Development)\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Node.js 18+ or 20+\n- npm\n\n### Steps\n```bash\n# 1. Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# 2. Initialize the local SQLite database\nnpx prisma db push\n\n# 3. Start the Next.js development server\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nVisit `http://localhost:3000` in your browser.\nCreate your personal account using the built-in modal to immediately begin chatting!\n\n---\n\n## 2. Server-Side API Key Configuration\n\nUMGN strictly keeps all API credentials server-side in `.env` or `.env.local`. Keys are **never transmitted to the client browser**.\n\nEdit `.env.local`:\n```env\n# Google Gemini API\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"AIzaSy...\"\n\n# OpenAI API (optional alternate)\nOPENAI_API_KEY=\"sk-proj-...\"\n\n# Production JWT Secret (must be minimum 32 characters)\nJWT_SECRET=\"your-ultra-secure-random-token-here\"\n```\n\n> **Note:** If no API key is set, UMGN runs with its built-in smart assistant engine so you can test features (streaming, chat history, markdown, data export, etc.) out-of-the-box.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Production HTTPS & Cloud Deployment\n\n### Option A: Docker Compose with Automatic HTTPS (Recommended)\nUMGN includes a ready-to-deploy multi-container setup with **Caddy**, which automatically provisions and manages free Let's Encrypt SSL/TLS certificates.\n\n1. **Deploy to a Cloud VPS** (AWS EC2, DigitalOcean Droplet, GCP Compute Engine, Hetzner, etc.):\n   - Ensure ports `80` and `443` are open in your cloud security firewall.\n   - Point your DNS A-record (e.g. `chat.yourdomain.com`) to your server's public IP.\n\n2. **Update `Caddyfile`**:\n   Replace `your-domain.com` with your actual domain and set your contact email.\n\n3. **Launch the stack**:\n   ```bash\n   docker-compose up -d --build\n   ```\n\nCaddy will automatically generate your HTTPS certificate and forward secure traffic to the Next.js container.\n\n### Option B: Standalone Node.js with Nginx\nIf running without Docker:\n```bash\n# Build the production bundle\nnpm run build\n\n# Run in production mode with PM2\nnpm install -g pm2\npm2 start npm --name \"umgn\" -- start\n```\nConfigure Nginx as a reverse proxy pointing to `http://127.0.0.1:3000` with Certbot for SSL.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Scaling Architecture (From 10 Users to 10,000+ Users)\n\n### Tier 1: 1–50 Users (Default SQLite Configuration)\n- Uses single-file SQLite database (`prisma/umgn.db`).\n- Zero maintenance, fast single-node queries, embedded directly on the server instance.\n- Automatic database backups can be taken by copying `prisma/umgn.db` to an S3 bucket or local snapshot directory.\n\n### Tier 2: 50–10,000+ Users (Cloud PostgreSQL & Redis)\nWhen scaling to a larger organization or public SaaS:\n\n1. **Switch Prisma to PostgreSQL**:\n   Open `prisma/schema.prisma` and update:\n   ```prisma\n   datasource db {\n     provider = \"postgresql\"\n     url      = env(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Update `.env` with your managed PostgreSQL URI** (Supabase, AWS RDS, Neon, or Railway):\n   ```env\n   DATABASE_URL=\"postgresql://postgres:password@db.supabase.co:5432/postgres?pgbouncer=true\"\n   ```\n3. **Push the schema to PostgreSQL**:\n   ```bash\n   npx prisma db push\n   ```\n4. **Horizontal Scaling**:\n   With stateless JWT cookies and an external database, you can run multiple instances of UMGN behind an AWS ALB or Cloudflare load balancer without sticky sessions.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Security & Privacy Features\n\n- **Data Minimization:** UMGN stores only `username`, `email`, and a 12-round salted `passwordHash`. No IP addresses, tracking pixels, or third-party analytics are stored.\n- **HttpOnly Cookies:** Authentication tokens are delivered as `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Strict`, `Secure` cookies, mitigating XSS token theft.\n- **Rate Limiting:** Built-in sliding-window rate limiters defend against credential stuffing, brute force logins, and API exhaustion.\n- **User Sovereignty (GDPR Compliant):**\n  - **Data Export:** Under *Settings > Data Controls*, users can download a complete JSON archive of all chats, messages, and settings.\n  - **Account Purge:** Users can permanently delete their account with cascade purging of all chat logs in a single transaction.\n- **Security Headers:** HSTS (Strict-Transport-Security), Content-Type-Options: nosniff, X-Frame-Options: DENY, and strict referrer policies enabled by default.\n","Description":"Create comprehensive production deployment and scaling guide for UMGN","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\LENOVO\\Documents\\ud\\DEPLOYMENT.md","toolAction":"Creating DEPLOYMENT.md","toolSummary":"Production deployment guide"}}]}
